From 858146fff04dcb66a3c9d6cbfbe0bcff301c6854 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alex Chong <achong@meta.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Mar 2026 16:07:49 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 55/63] [cuttlefish] Add --instance_num flag to stop_cvd for
 single-instance stop

Summary:
# Motivation:
We want to make launching and stopping emulators on macOS for multi-constellation easy. Keeping track of base_instance_num argument is not easy for users and over-complicates things. The current device implementation leads to race conditions where devices fail to launch.

Adding an instance registry with atomic operations allows us to provide an easy start/stop interface to users running multiple emulators.
# Overview:

Add --instance_num flag to stop_cvd for stopping a single instance via the
instance registry, enabling independent lifecycle management.

When --instance_num=N is set:
- Load config from the registry for that specific instance
- Stop only that instance and unregister it from the registry
- Other running instances are unaffected

When --instance_num is not set (default, stop all):
- Try monolithic config first (existing behavior)
- If no monolithic config exists, fall back to the registry: list all
  registered instances and stop each one
- For instances whose config can't be loaded, fall back to SIGKILL
